        "original_id": "b856bdc1-df9b-5d8c-b6b6-da57acf701fb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jerry Bruckheimer, Boaz Yakin, Christopher Lloyd, Jeff Daniels, Daryl Hannah, Elizabeth Hurley, Wallace Shawn, Ray Walston, Herman Boone, Denzel Washington\n- Films: Remember the Titans, My Favorite Martian\n- TV Series: My Favorite Martian\n- Organizations: T. C. Williams High School football team\n- Topics: film production, casting, box office, sports coaching\n\nFacts:\n- Herman Boone was born on October 28, 1935.\n- Herman Boone coached the 1971 T. C. Williams High School football team to a 13-0 season, a state championship, and a national championship runner-up finish.\n- Herman Boone’s coaching of the 1971 T. C. Williams High School football team was the basis for the 2000 film Remember the Titans.\n- Remember the Titans is a 2000 American sports film produced by Jerry Bruckheimer and directed by Boaz Yakin.\n- In Remember the Titans, Denzel Washington portrayed Herman Boone.\n- My Favorite Martian is a 1999 American science fiction comedy film based on the 1960s television series My Favorite Martian.\n- Ray Walston had starred in the 1960s television series My Favorite Martian before appearing in the 1999 film adaptation.\n- My Favorite Martian stars Christopher Lloyd, Jeff Daniels, Daryl Hannah, Elizabeth Hurley, Wallace Shawn, and Ray Walston.\n- My Favorite Martian grossed $36.8 million domestically against a $65 million budget.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
